## Issues Identified & Fixed

### 1. Scheduler Version Conflicts ❌→✅
**Problem:** Multiple scheduler versions causing potential conflicts
- React DOM installed scheduler@0.23.2
- Root node_modules had scheduler@0.25.0-rc (release candidate)
- Version mismatch could cause runtime errors

**Solution:**
- Pinned React and React-DOM to exact version `18.3.1`
- Removed problematic React alias configuration in vite.config.js
- Maintained dependency deduplication for clean resolution

### 2. rollup-plugin-visualizer Issues ❌→✅
**Problem:** Plugin causing "Access is denied" errors and build instability
- Plugin was installed but not properly integrated
- Native binary dependencies causing file access issues on Windows
- No actual bundle visualization needed for production

**Solution:**
- Completely removed `rollup-plugin-visualizer` from package.json
- Cleaned up any references in build configuration
- Build now runs without permission issues

### 3. Vite Configuration Complexity ❌→✅
**Problem:** Overly complex Vite configuration causing build failures
- Too many manual chunking rules causing HTML proxy errors
- Unnecessary alias configurations for React/React-DOM
- Complex terser configuration slowing builds

**Solution:**
- Simplified manual chunking strategy
- Added `vite-plugin-html` for proper HTML handling
- Optimized build target to `es2015` for better browser support
- Removed problematic plugin configurations

